From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: control pipe client (IPC contract, role "worker")

Implement the child side of SplitPlay's docs/contracts/ipc.md, protocol 1:

- New options --pipe <name> and --desk <id> (also --name=value). --desk
  must match [a-z0-9-]{1,32}; --pipe requires --desk. Without --pipe the
  worker runs standalone as before.
- Right after the signal handlers are installed, main() opens the pipe
  (overlapped I/O, SECURITY_IDENTIFICATION), sends hello (protocol, role,
  desk, pid, version, session) and waits up to 10 s for welcome. A failed
  handshake exits with code 3.
- After the HTTP/RTSP threads start, the worker waits (up to 10 s) for the
  HTTP base port to accept loopback connections and sends ready with
  ports.base.
- A heartbeat thread sends heartbeat every 1000 ms with state
  starting/idle/streaming and the contract metrics keys; clients is the
  number of active RTSP sessions, the encoder metrics stay 0 until Stage 3.
- Requests: shutdown answers ok and exits through
  lifetime::exit_sunshine(0); pair, list_clients and unpair map to
  nvhttp::pin, nvhttp::get_all_clients and nvhttp::unpair_client;
  set_profile and send_sas answer "unsupported"; other requests with an id
  answer "unknown_type". Lines over 64 KiB are dropped.
- If the pipe breaks the worker exits with code 3: it never runs
  unsupervised.
- The MIT contract headers from SplitPlay native/include/splitplay are
  included from third-party/splitplay/include (copied unmodified by
  worker/scripts/fetch.sh; SPLITPLAY_CONTRACTS_INCLUDE_DIR overrides it).
  trace.h's sp_desk_hash() is logged as the desk's trace hash.

